WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.930
Imu-Sama, the secret ruler of the World Government,
probably has the most mind-boggling power

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.080
in all of One Piece.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:14.660
If you thought the Nika fruit was overpowered,
then Imu is about to be straight up broken,

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.920
with one of the strongest devil fruit powers
imaginable.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:24.180
If we’re right, then Imu is firmly in One
Piece final boss territory.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.679
The King of the Pirates is the person with
the most freedom on the sea.

00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:33.950
But little does Luffy know - little does the
world know, that there is a true king in the

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.340
One Piece world - and that no one is free.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.450
If anyone is to claim the One Piece, it’s
not the rival members of the Worst Generation

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.580
they have to worry about, nor the fearsome
Yonkou.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:52.070
Not even the almighty Cross Guild is the biggest
threat on the Grand Line, despite having the

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:57.060
greatest swordsman in the world (and greatest
clown in the world) among their number.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:03.191
The faction that has the most to lose from
the One Piece being discovered is the World

00:01:03.191 --> 00:01:04.191
Government.

00:01:04.191 --> 00:01:09.939
The future Fleet Admiral, Sakazuki, didn’t
think twice about condemning an entire island

00:01:09.939 --> 00:01:15.560
to a fiery death if it meant restricting the
knowledge of the poneglyphs - the objects

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.950
that reveal the true history and lead to the
ultimate treasure.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:26.119
They’d even imprison one of their own CP-9
agents - Who’s Who - for losing the Nika

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:32.610
fruit, which is somehow connected to the legacy
of Joyboy.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:38.710
It’s obvious that the World Government will
do anything to stop this treasure from being

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:45.890
revealed - and at the top of that government,
at the top of the whole world, is not a pirate

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:50.170
king: that seat has long sat vacant since
Roger’s execution.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:56.689
The person with the most power in the One
Piece world, even if most of the world doesn’t

00:01:56.689 --> 00:01:59.719
know it, is the mysterious Imu-Sama.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:05.029
And chances are that this mysterious entity
will pull out all the stops in order to prevent

00:02:05.029 --> 00:02:09.849
any pirates from claiming the One Piece and
learning the true history.

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:13.420
There are a lot of candidates for who will
be Luffy’s final opponent.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.780
Could it be Akainu?

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:15.780
Or Blackbeard?

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.500
Or the infamous Buggy D. Clown?

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.010
We actually made a whole video about it that
you can check out here: Only time will tell

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:30.379
who Luffy’s final match up will be, but
it Im-Sama is one of the prime candidates.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:37.340
The world government has been one of the story’s
leading antagonistic forces even since the

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.370
earliest chapters in East Blue.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:44.060
If the final opponent ends up being the World
Government and not another pirate crew like

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:49.560
Blackbeard or Shanks, the most likely big
bad could be Imu.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:54.390
Even though Luffy has a personal grudge against
Akainu, Imu-Sama is the ultimate leader of

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.390
the world government.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:02.870
And if Luffy represents the the new dawn of
the world, if he beats the drums of liberation,

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:09.240
and bring freedom to the world - then Im may
represent the opposite, the highest authority

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:15.340
in the world, putting people across the seas
in chains, both literal and metaphorical.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:21.840
But if Im is a fighter worthy of occupying
the spot of Luffy’s final opponent, then

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:28.260
they need to give us one hell of a fight and
he needs a power set that contends with the

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:31.530
wild abilities of the Sun God Nika fruit.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:37.579
One of the prevailing theories of Nika’s
fruit is that they have the most overpowered

00:03:37.579 --> 00:03:39.530
fruit possible: the water-water fruit.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.739
Or the Sea-Sea fruit- Or Ocean-Ocean.

00:03:41.739 --> 00:03:47.349
Or the fruit of some unnamed Sea God - whatever
you call it, it’s the wettest fruit around

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:56.010
- pure water as opposed to muddy water like
Caribou’s swamp or cold water like Kuzan’s

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.620
ice.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.439
Devil fruit users all lose the ability to
swim.

00:04:01.439 --> 00:04:08.060
The sea drains them of their abilities, and
even the ability to move while submerged.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:13.109
Someone with a water-water fruit would be
a natural counter not only to something like

00:04:13.109 --> 00:04:14.230
the Mera-Mera no Mi.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.780
Luffy’s hard counter to Eneru’s lightning
fruit was one thing, but we’re talking about

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.000
a hard counter to every.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.000
Single.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.000
Devil fruit.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:28.120
If we think that the Nika fruit seems OP,
with its abilities to seemingly break reality

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:33.810
and apply cartoon logic to Luffy’s stretching
and shape shifting, then get ready to get

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:41.580
a whole lot OP-er, when Imu-Sama simply turns
off his devil fruit with a nice soak.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:47.560
Besides the idea that a water fruit would
just be absurdly broken, it would make a lot

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:49.160
of sense for Imu-Sama to have.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.400
The Japanese word “Umi” means “sea”
or “ocean”.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.840
Umi backwards spells “Imu” = Coincidence?

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.430
Probably not, given how much Oda loves wordplay.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:02.870
It’s too on the nose to not have a meaning.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:06.949
Thematically, Imu having a sea fruit makes
sense as well.

00:05:06.949 --> 00:05:10.580
He is the being with the most power on the
seas.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:16.030
The dangerous oceans of the One Piece world
are what keep people separated, isolated from

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:20.340
each other on their individual islands.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:28.190
Only by braving the treacherous tides and
turbulent weather of the Grand Line can members

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:32.640
of different countries connect politically
and economically.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:38.900
This separation makes it all the easier for
the World Government to exert control over

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:44.150
the seas, especially given their monopoly
on Kairoseki - sea stone - that allows their

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:49.539
ships to move safely through the calm belt,
bypassing its deadly sea kings.

00:05:49.539 --> 00:05:55.530
If Imu-Sama controls the oceans in a figurative
sense, maybe his fruit allows him to control

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.580
the oceans in a much more literal sense.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:04.440
However - this isn’t the only power that
would make sense for this all powerful figure

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.750
of the One Piece world.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:11.260
If Imu is “Umi” backwards - maybe he’s
not the ocean at all.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:14.210
Maybe he’s the opposite of the ocean.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:19.860
And a lot of the time when we’re thinking
about elemental powers, we think of water

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:21.610
and fire being opposites.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:27.650
But in the context of One Piece, I don’t
think fire really makes sense as the opposite

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:31.120
of the ocean.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.650
In One Piece, you’re either at sea…or
you’re on land.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:41.080
We’ve seen Pica’s stone fruit and Crocodile’s
sand fruit - we even had Miss Merry Chirstmas’s

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:46.729
tunneling mole fruit, but we have yet to see
a proper Earth-Earth fruit in the series.

00:06:46.729 --> 00:06:51.720
The closest may be the Revolutionary Commander
Morley’s Oshi Oshi no Mi, which allows her

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:55.289
to push the ground and mold it as if it were
clay.

00:06:55.289 --> 00:07:00.889
However, this fruit is a paramecia - we’re
still missing an Earth logia in a club that

00:07:00.889 --> 00:07:05.169
includes other elements like fire, ice, and
so on.

00:07:05.169 --> 00:07:10.150
Speaking of Morley, though - did you know
that this revolutionary has a bounty of 293,

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.470
000, 000 berries.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:14.770
Impressive and befitting one of the most wanted
people in the world.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:20.600
It’s far more than the slithering slime-man,
Trebol’s 99, 000, 000 berry bounty.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:25.610
With your help, though, you can help our channel
to overtake Trebol and raise our bounty by

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:29.569
hitting the subscribe button!

00:07:29.569 --> 00:07:34.800
The Earth fruit doesn’t feel as overpowered
as something like a sea fruit - but it also

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.000
feels a lot more likely to exist.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:43.690
If devil fruit users are cursed by the sea,
and the sea is their ultimate weakness, it

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:47.270
might not make much sense for there to be
a sea fruit after all.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:53.440
And we can’t really discard Earth - as one
of the four classical elements, it would definitely

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:57.009
still pack a punch as a devil fruit.

00:07:57.009 --> 00:08:00.599
Having the earth fruit would make a lot of
thematic sense for Imu as well.

00:08:00.599 --> 00:08:06.000
For pirates like Luffy, setting out to sea
is representative of finding freedom and adventure.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.520
It’s the opposite of being trapped on the
land - like Luffy was for so long when he

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.950
was too young to set sail with Ace or Shanks.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:20.270
If the open sea gives pirates freedom, then
the earth or the land represents the opposite.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:25.310
Where else but the land do the Straw Hats
find corrupt kingdoms and monarchies like

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:30.560
that of Wapol - when pirates like Arlong,
Crocodile, and Doflamingo gave up adventuring

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:35.330
on the sea, they turned to dominating others
on islands.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:41.010
Imu having the earth fruit would also solve
one of the biggest mysteries in One Piece:

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:42.840
Who created the Red Line?

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:48.620
Back when Luffy’s fruit was still thought
to be just a rubber fruit, he showed us how

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:53.709
a creative, strong, and willful fruit user
can turn even an average fruit into a force

00:08:53.709 --> 00:08:55.570
to be reckoned with.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:09:02.490
The Earth fruit may not seem overpowered at
first glance, but imagine if Imu is powerful

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:05.390
enough to create a continent.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:13.170
If Imu was alive during the void century,
perhaps he’s the reason there are no continents,

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.450
save the Red Line.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:19.490
Using an Earth fruit, Imu-Sama could have
reshaped the world to their liking.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:24.220
Landmasses could have been sunk, leaving the
human population disparate and scattered across

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:25.220
distant islands.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:31.670
The red line could have been erected, bordering
seas from each other and restricting travel

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.080
between parts of the globe.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:38.029
Imu’s home itself, Mariejois, even sits
atop this mighty landmass.

00:09:38.029 --> 00:09:44.870
If this is Imu’s power, then Luffy will
need a fruit as OP as the Nika fruit to even

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:48.430
stand a chance.

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:54.000
However, water and earth aren’t the only
options for Imu’s potential power, either.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:59.330
There could be a To-Be-Determined mythical
zoan to rival the Nika fruit - maybe a Sea

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:04.279
God fruit or, while we speculated in a previous
video - that you can watch here - that Blackbeard

00:10:04.279 --> 00:10:10.690
possesses a Moon God fruit, maybe Imu-Sama
is the real Moon God instead.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:18.150
If Oda does have Imu as a final villain instead
of Blackbeard, this could be very fitting.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:24.530
And after seeing Shanks’ incredible feat
of conqueror’s haki in chapter 1055, we

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:29.990
have to wonder if Imu even needs a devil fruit
at all.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:35.839
Perhaps, like Shanks, Imu-Sama is just a haki
user.

00:10:35.839 --> 00:10:42.430
However, one has to wonder how strong is the
conqueror’s haki of someone who has literally

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:44.990
conquered the entire globe.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:50.820
Shanks’ haki stopped Aramaki in his tracks
from miles away off the coast of Wano - could

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:53.900
Imu’s haki have an even farther reach?

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:57.610
There’s also the matter of the saber that
Imu carries.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:03.110
So far we’ve only seen them use it to tear
up bounty posters, in order to let the Gorosei

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:05.670
know which lights need to be extinguished.

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:11.490
We have to wonder, though, if maybe that’s
not all that sword is good for.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:16.480
Luffy is particularly susceptible to cutting,
slashing, and stabbing attacks - but this

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:19.630
would be a strange route for Oda to go down.

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:24.180
Either Mihawk isn’t actually the strongest
swordsman in the world and it’s Imu instead,

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:30.910
or Zoro would end up with a more powerful
opponent than Luffy’s in the final war.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:38.519
Finally, though, we have the somewhat anti-climactic
option.

00:11:38.519 --> 00:11:40.839
Imu might just not be a fighter.

00:11:40.839 --> 00:11:45.120
It wouldn’t be the first time that a major
antagonist wasn’t a combatant.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:49.641
In Water 7/Enies Lobby, one of the other notable
times the Straw Hats went up against the World

00:11:49.641 --> 00:11:55.839
Government directly, the leader of CP9 and
arguably the central villain was Spandam.

00:11:55.839 --> 00:12:02.800
Spandam, despite his special sword, Funkfreed,
was not a fighter.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:08.100
This incompetent, sniveling, utterly punchable
Cipher-Pol operative relied on the muscle

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:15.130
of Rob Lucci and Lucci ended up becoming Luffy’s
primary opponent for the arc.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:19.760
It might be the case that Imu-Sama, like most
Celestial Dragons, just relies on the military

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:23.720
might of the marines to carry out his will
and for protection.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:29.160
It could be that the Gorosei serve as Imu’s
elite guard - though it isn’t yet confirmed

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.020
that they’re fighters either.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:40.089
We just really, really hope we get to see
Ghandi break out that sword.

00:12:40.089 --> 00:12:45.660
It’s unclear what Imu’s role in the story
will be, but after their introduction at the

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:51.730
Reverie, it’s clear that they’ll play
a pivotal role in the final saga.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:56.050
We still need to learn what the Great Cleansing
is - and to learn how the World Government

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.690
plans to carry it out.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:03.389
Maybe the Marines’ secret weapon, the SSG,
will play some part.

00:13:03.389 --> 00:13:09.060
But with so little One Piece left, here’s
to hoping that Oda can pack in as many wild

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:11.930
fights and earth-shattering revelations as
possible.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:16.149
And if you track of all the poeple luffy still
has to punch before the end of the story and

00:13:16.149 --> 00:13:20.060
why, you should watch this video here next.

